# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD runs hs-start.sh, which boots rsyslog/cron, starts sshd,
# starts nginx in daemon (background) mode, then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * nginx (:80) and sshd (:22) are ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts —
#     the HTTP header / ssh-login probes exercise live subsystems, and "fixed
#     the config but never reloaded nginx" stays detectable;
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so reloading/restarting nginx cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RELOAD/RESTART nginx after editing
# nginx.conf, not merely start it if absent.
